# A3 step 6 T30-0 "Fakten + Op-Weg" (design ws-10/cli-grp/a3-schritt6/DESIGN-T30-MANAGER-DIREKTIVEN-20261109.md v1.1, row T30-0 of
# section 7; owner standing approval, default 0, NO behaviour change). Measurement only: the bots post facts, the manager stores
# and counts them, the manager's op path exists without a caller. This contract pins:
#   (a) the gate: status, edge and wish go out only from PlayerbotAI::PostManagerStatus, reached only through the status hook
#       (StatusSeconds && group_mgr::Applies(Manager)); no OwnsBot, no .Types key, no IsManaged in T30-0 (m1);
#   (b) own reads only (M6): ManagerFacts.{h,cpp} and PostManagerStatus read the bot itself - no member list, no other Player*,
#       no other bot's AI, no write; every Player* there is the bot; the ad-hoc helpers they call read only their argument;
#       the interim wish uses the S7 scan rule (IsGroupHelpQuest, Waits, the same open-objective test, F3 (a));
#   (c) the op path (3.5): OpSource::Manager appended, the join bits, QueueManagerJoin/QueueManagerLeave/ReadManagerOpCounts/
#       TakeManagerOutcomes declared and defined with NO caller; the outcomes counted in Drain around Run (m3) - the Run*
#       bodies, the dispatcher and FlushMinute ([GroupOps]/[GroupWrite]) stay byte-identical (SHA256 pins);
#   (d) the manager: no op, no directive, no supervisor postbox; pass order drain -> tables -> shadow count -> minute line;
#       Status/GroupEdge/GroupWish into their tables, a status drops the bot's old wish; shadow candidates via
#       supervisor::Applies and StaleMs(StatusSeconds);
#   (e) no supervisor::Post/Drain/Forget anywhere in the pair's files;
#   (f) the unit tests cover the new pure helpers.
# T30-1 (directives, a3s6_t30_directives pins the new parts) moves these pins: the hook also posts for a bot the manager holds
# (|| IsManaged; OwnsBot/Types/Blocks are allowed from T30-1 on), ReadFlags uses the gate-free CandidateFacts, the manager is
# the one caller of QueueManagerJoin/QueueManagerLeave/TakeManagerOutcomes and posts directives through the one R10-gated
# supervisor::Post, RunJoin reads the join bits (H_RUN_JOIN re-pinned), the shadow lambda takes the R10 form.
# Pure rules: t/manager_inbox_policy_tests.cpp, t/group_op_queue_tests.cpp. Every check_* returns "" when it holds, else the
# reason; the negative probes at the end reuse them on mutated text.
